# Space CODEOWNERS (§4.2, D-011): gated paths ONLY.
#
# /<system>/provides/** entries do NOT belong here at template time — each
# system's onboarding PR adds its own entry when it joins (US-102, §9.2
# step 2). Pre-seeding a system entry here would be a layout invention this
# template does not make.
#
# ── AN OWNER THAT DOES NOT EXIST IS IGNORED, NOT REJECTED ─────────────────
#
# GitHub does not refuse an unknown owner; it drops the line. So a CODEOWNERS
# that names a team nobody created LOOKS like it gates `/space.yaml` and gates
# nothing — and that matters more than it sounds: code-owner review is the
# whole of the G4 safety argument (BRANCH-PROTECTION.md), and this file is its
# only mechanism. An inert CODEOWNERS is an ungated trust root.
#
# The placeholders below are therefore SINGLE LOGINS, not `@org/team`. That is
# a deliberate change made on 2026-07-26 after walking this template from zero:
# the previous placeholder was `@REPLACE_WITH_ORG/REPLACE_WITH_TEAM_OR_LOGIN`
# with an instruction to replace both halves — and replacing both halves
# literally produces `@your-org/your-login`, which is a TEAM reference to a
# team that does not exist. The instruction was followed exactly and still
# produced an inert file. A shape that cannot be filled in wrongly beats a
# warning about filling it in wrongly.
#
# Individual logins are also what a small space actually wants:
#
#   /space.yaml     @alice
#   /decisions/**   @alice @bob
#
# A TEAM is legal too — `@my-org/space-admins` — but only if you have
# confirmed it exists, is publicly visible, and has write access to this repo.
# All three are required; GitHub ignores the line if any is missing.
#
# ── VERIFY IT, DO NOT EYEBALL IT ──────────────────────────────────────────
#
# GitHub exposes exactly this, with line numbers:
#
#   gh api repos/OWNER/REPO/codeowners/errors
#
# An empty `errors` array means every owner here resolves. `a2a doctor` runs
# this for you (the `codeowners resolvable` row) — it is the difference between
# a trust root you checked and one you assumed.

/space.yaml     @REPLACE_WITH_LOGIN
/decisions/**   @REPLACE_WITH_LOGIN
